READING
====================================================================================================
  logprob                AUC 0.704
  self-report            AUC 0.628
  self-report, falsified AUC 0.372   <- the attack drives it below chance
  gap, logprob - self-report: +0.076

  Falsification pushes the self-report below chance (0.5) on 18 of 19 powered cells. The logprob surface is unchanged by that attack by construction -- it is not the surface the attack writes to -- which is the protocol claim: a receiver should weight on a surface the sender does not author.

  R3: the self-report is also simply absent at times -- up to 33.0% of rows on mmlu/phi4_mini_reasoning. A surface an agent may decline to provide is a weaker commitment than one derived from tokens it already emitted.

  Weak-tier arm, separately (11 powered cells): logprob 0.708, self-report 0.572, falsified 0.428. Same direction, so the protocol property is not an artefact of model strength.

